messages:
maria-ss: hi @sam-cs — got an escalation from a customer saying they're seeing sudden 429s and timeouts when they burst test. they say it worked fine yesterday and only started after they turned on higher concurrency.

sam-cs: thanks — which customer? any repro steps or request ids?

customer-infra: it's acme-cloud (reported via support ticket #9876). reproduction: simple loop of 200 parallel requests over 30s, each request is a normal text generation POST to /v1/generate. they used our JS SDK v0.9.1 defaults.

maria-ss: ok can you paste the SDK config they used? esp retry settings and whether they set Idempotency-Key?

customer-infra: they didn't set Idempotency-Key. SDK call looked like:
```js
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
await Promise.all(Array.from({length:200}).map(() => client.generate({ model: 'rw-medium', prompt: 'hello' })));
```
no special retry or throttle config.

aj-plat: quick notes — default SDK behavior in v0.9.1: 2 retries on network errors, backs off with base 250ms exponential, uses full-jitter. it does NOT inject Idempotency-Key automatically for generate calls. it will respect 429 Retry-After header if present.

devops-bot: observing throttle events in prod for that tenant around 2026-03-15T14:05Z — rate limiter dropped ~18% of requests as quota/outright burst protection. logs: 
```
RATE_LIMIT DROP tenant=acme-cloud route=/v1/generate tokens=3500 limit=3000 window=60s
HTTP 429 X-Request-Id=req_0a1b2c3d
```

sam-cs: that matches their windowed burst. they saturated token bucket and hit burst cap; some requests may have been rejected before SDK could retry (parallel requests).

maria-ss: guidance to provide: (1) recommend client-side concurrency limits, (2) enable Idempotency-Key for safety if they want retries, (3) tune SDK retry/jitter and consider slower ramp-up when bursting, (4) examine Dedicated/reserved capacity if steady high qps.

aj-plat: also point out that for idempotency: server-side accepted idempotency header is `Idempotency-Key`. if they add it the SDK retries won't duplicate side-effecting operations. generation endpoints are usually safe-but-costly; duplicates mean extra tokens billed.

customer-infra: can you give a concrete reproducible test we can run to confirm? they'd like a client-side script that simulates the problem but handles retries correctly.

maria-ss: here's a minimal repro script (node) — shows naive burst then a controlled run with concurrency limit and idempotency header:
```js
// naive-burst.js - will hit rate limits
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/sdk');
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
await Promise.all(Array.from({length:200}).map(() => client.generate({ model: 'rw-medium', prompt:'x'.repeat(50) })));
```

```js
// polite-run.js - uses limited concurrency, idempotency and retry backoff
const pLimit = require('p-limit');
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/sdk');
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, maxRetries: 5, retryBaseMs: 200 });
const limit = pLimit(20); // cap concurrency to 20
const tasks = Array.from({length:200}).map((_,i) => limit(() => {
  const idKey = `acme-${Date.now()}-${i}`;
  return client.generate({ model:'rw-medium', prompt:'x'.repeat(50), headers: { 'Idempotency-Key': idKey } });
}));
await Promise.all(tasks);
```

aj-plat: note: we added `maxRetries` and `retryBaseMs` — those are SDK options in 0.9.x. maxRetries=5 + full-jitter should smear retries and avoid thundering herd.

sam-cs: add advice for parsing `Retry-After` and honoring it for 429s. if Retry-After is present, the client should back off at least that long before retrying that request.

maria-ss: also mention billing impact: duplicates from retries without idempotency will incur extra token usage. pinging billing-bot to attach cost estimate for a 200-request burst with 18% duplicates.

billing-bot: estimated extra tokens = ~200k tokens, cost delta ~$12 for that burst (rough estimate), will send formal calc to the customer.

customer-infra: great. one more: are there SDK defaults we recommend they change globally? they'd like a safe baseline for all clients.

aj-plat: recommended baseline: maxRetries=3-5, retryBaseMs=150-300ms, jitter=full, concurrency cap per process 10-50 depending on instance size, always set Idempotency-Key for operations that can be retried without business side-effects or where dedupe is acceptable, and instrument Retry-After handling.

maria-ss: i'll draft a reply to the ticket with repro scripts, suggested SDK config, and a note about moving to Dedicated if they need predictable burst headroom. cc @aj-plat for the SDK snippets.

sam-cs: thanks — also add a small server-side mitigation note: we can provide tenant-scoped burst allowance increases for short-term load tests if they coordinate with support 24h in advance.

customer-infra: thanks all, we'll run the polite-run and report back. :thumbsup:

maria-ss: closing loop: run polite-run, check logs for 200s, if still seeing 429 please include `X-Request-Id` from responses and send to support so infra can trace.
